  "notes": "Prompt API sampling parameters (temperature, topK, LanguageModel.params()) were exposed to web pages in Chrome 148 only through the AIPromptAPIParams origin trial (M148 branch 7778: AIPromptAPIParams implies AIPromptAPILegacyParams; desktop OSes only). Since then the spec and Chromium main deprecate the raw parameters (extension contexts only) in favour of samplingMode; the ChromeStatus record for this id is now titled 'Prompt API Sampling Mode' and the milestone=148 listing name changed to match (slug kept per the durable-route contract). samplingMode is documented on-page as a successor note but is NOT inventoried here because the M148 branch IDL has no samplingMode member. BCD api/LanguageModel.json carries the parent interface only (Chrome 148, Edge 138 behind a flag); webstatus.dev languagemodel = limited.",
  "outOfScope": [
    {
      "name": "samplingMode",
      "rationale": "Successor API quoted for context only: the Chromium M148 branch (7778) IDL has no samplingMode member, so it is not part of the Chrome 148 surface this page documents; a separate additive page is a follow-up goal."
    },
    {
      "name": "create",
      "rationale": "Pre-existing Prompt API factory quoted only as the call site that receives the temperature/topK options; it belongs to the parent Prompt API feature (ChromeStatus 5134603979063296), not this sampling-parameters change."
    },
    {
      "name": "availability",
      "rationale": "Pre-existing Prompt API availability check quoted only because it accepts LanguageModelCreateCoreOptions; it belongs to the parent Prompt API feature, not this sampling-parameters change."
    }
  ]
